{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "12", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "06", "M": "45", "S": "01"}}, "news": [{"title": "Bombay HC clears construction on two Pune Cantonment leasehold plots", "para": "The Bombay High Court has permitted residential building on leasehold plots in Pune Cantonment, mandating that defence authorities grant construction permits within a month. The ruling emphasizes that future defence requirements cannot compromise the rights of current leaseholders. These leases remain in effect until 2033, but renewals are uncertain. Meanwhile, defence authorities are considering legal avenues to contest this decision.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/bombay-hc-clears-construction-on-two-pune-cantonment-leasehold-plots/134113434?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-368012/134113434.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Redevelopment gains can\u2019t be taxed in hands of CHS, rules Mumbai ITAT", "para": "The Mumbai ITAT has annulled a contentious Rs 18.4 crore tax addition for a housing society, stating the society served merely as a representative for its flat owners. The tribunal observed that the transactions reported under the society's PAN weren't its own revenues, given that no sale proceeds appeared in its bank account. This decision will benefit housing societies engaged in redevelopment projects.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/redevelopment-gains-cant-be-taxed-in-hands-of-chs-rules-mumbai-itat/134107186?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-51224/134107186.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Buildings \u2018unsafe\u2019 for years, Noida authority now pastes vacate notices after Satya Niketan collapse", "para": "The Noida Authority is issuing vacate notices for 56 unsafe buildings that have been flagged as dilapidated for years. With these structures situated in crowded neighborhoods, residents are left in a state of uncertainty. Following a severe collapse in 2018, the authority had initially conducted a survey, highlighting numerous unauthorized buildings. Previous demolition efforts were largely ineffective, leading to current notices being sent for many of the same properties.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/buildings-unsafe-for-years-noida-authority-now-pastes-vacate-notices-after-satya-niketan-collapse/134107101?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-249916/134107101.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}